{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1791473690-nL7xghRPSo3mQfUR6VfK","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found the cause, but I haven't changed anything because the code doesn't say what the correct host is.\n\n`src/weather.js:1` hardcodes `https://api.weather.invalid/v1/today?...`. The `.invalid` TLD is reserved and never resolves, so `fetch` fails with `ENOTFOUND` and the widget gets no data. The API key isn't the problem, because the request never reaches a server. Nothing else in the repo (`server.js`, `doctor.sh`, `package.json`) names the real weather provider or its base URL.\n\nTwo ways to fix it:\n1. If you tell me the real API host, I'll put it in `src/weather.js`.\n2. Alternatively, I can read the base URL from an env var such as `WEATHER_API_URL`, so the host isn't hardcoded. You'd then set it wherever `WEATHER_API_KEY` is managed.\n\nOnce the host is right, there may be further problems, such as the endpoint path, the `key` query param, or the response shape. I'll re-run `npm run weather` after the change to check.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":39664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":711,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Claude Platform on AWS","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a9e993a-4132-4bb3-b9b0-002bf5009ea7","uuid":"8a771816-b810-4f6a-9392-4401c1cdc345","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:34:55.207Z","request_id":"gen-1791473690-nL7xghRPSo3mQfUR6VfK"}
